# GymFlow marketing site — environment variables
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Everything here is optional: the site builds and runs with no variables at all.
# Vite reads these at BUILD time and bakes them into the bundle, so on your host
# they must be set as build variables, not runtime ones. Anything prefixed VITE_
# is public (it ships in the page source). Never put a secret here.

# Microsoft Clarity project ID (heatmaps and session recordings).
# clarity.microsoft.com → your project → Settings → Overview.
# Clarity only loads in production builds, and only after the visitor allows it in
# the cookie banner. Leave blank to turn it off.
VITE_CLARITY_PROJECT_ID=

# Google Analytics is not configured here. Its measurement ID is in the last
# <script> of the <head> in index.html, limited to the gymflow.sbs hostname.
# Replace both with your own. See README.md → "Making it yours".
